   "evidence": "In Mathlib, `changeGenerator` (Mathlib/Algebra/QuadraticAlgebra/Basic.lean:468) is `lift` at `u \u2022 \u03c9 + k`. For `x + y\u03c9 \u21a6 (x + ky) + uy\u03c9`: the trace is `2x + 2ky + buy = 2x + (ub + 2k)y = 2x + b'y`, and the norm is `x\u00b2 + (ub + 2k)xy \u2212 (u\u00b2a \u2212 ubk \u2212 k\u00b2)y\u00b2 = x\u00b2 + b'xy \u2212 a'y\u00b2`. Both identities use only `ha`, `hb`. Mathlib's `norm_algHom`/`trace_algHom`/`algHom_star` (AlgHom.lean:103\u2013114) need `Function.Injective`, so the injectivity-free general versions are missing and natural to add.",
   "file": "TauCeti/NumberTheory/QuadraticOrder/IndexTwo.lean",
   "fix": "Add `star_changeGenerator`, `norm_changeGenerator`, `trace_changeGenerator` and `mapRingHom_changeGenerator` for arbitrary `a b u k` with `ha hb`, in the `TauCeti/Algebra/QuadraticAlgebra` layer. Then derive the four `algHomDiscrZero` lemmas as one-line specializations, or drop them.",
   "issue": "`star_algHomDiscrZero`, `norm_algHomDiscrZero` (l.130), `trace_algHomDiscrZero` (l.137) and `mapRingHom_algHomDiscrZero` (l.145) are computations proved only for the special case `u = 2`, `k = -b`. The same computation works for any `changeGenerator a b u k ha hb`: with `ha`, `hb` alone, trace, norm and conjugation are preserved and the map commutes with `mapRingHom`, even without injectivity. Tau Ceti already applies `changeGenerator`/`changeGeneratorEquiv` in `Algebra/QuadraticAlgebra/{Split,DualNumber,AlgEquiv}.lean`, `NumberTheory/QuadraticOrder/Field.lean` and `HilbertSymbol/NormSubgroup.lean`.",
   "line": 123
  }
 ],
